 34CL c  {+34}S+1p|)1n+{+34}Cl from J|p=0+ {+34}S ground state.                 
 34CL c  2009Pa28: a 25-MeV {+3}He beam was produced from the MP tandem         
 34CL2c  accelerator at MLL, Garching, Germany and impinged on 50-|mg/cm{+2},   
 34CL3c  99.999% {+34}S-enriched Ag{-2}S targets. Light reaction products were  
 34CL4c  momentum-analyzed in the Q3D magnetic spectrograph at |q{-lab}=15|' and
 34CL5c  25|' and detected by a multiwire gas proportional counter backed by a  
 34CL6c  plastic scintillator with FWHM=10 keV. Measured trition spectra.       
 34CL7c  Deduced resonances and {+33}S(p,|g){+34}Cl reaction rate at relevant   
 34CL8c  nova temperatures. Conference proceedings: 2011PaZV, 2010PaZT.         
 34CL c  2007Fu06: a 140-MeV/nucleon {+3}He beam was produced from K400 Ring    
 34CL2c  cyclotron at RCNP, Osaka University and impinged on a 93.47%-enriched  
 34CL3c  3.3-mg/cm{+2} {+34}S self-supporting target. The outgoing tritons were 
 34CL4c  momentum analyzed by the Grand Raiden spectrometer at 0 |' and detected
 34CL5c  using a focal-plane detector system with FWHM=21 keV. Measured         
 34CL6c  |s(E{-t},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfer, B(GT) and compared    
 34CL7c  with DWBA and Shell-model calculations.                                
 34CL cL E$From 2009Pa28, unless otherwise noted. An overall statistical        
 34CL2cL uncertainty of 2 keV and a systematic uncertainty of 3 keV (2009Pa28)  
 34CL3cL are added in quadrature by evaluators, unless otherwise noted.         
